From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NorkzYT <richard@pcscorp.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:06:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): typed dev_test_run tool, scanner recovery and
 test-credential guards

Kanban workers run as -q sessions, so the unattended gate denies a Tirith
warn: the operator-approved `PGPASSFILE=... MATCHING_TEST_DATABASE_URL=
'postgresql://postgres@127.0.0.1:55443/...' go test` command is rejected
(raw_ip_url + schemeless_to_sink, MEDIUM; incident t_12595b96 run 370) and
the worker had no approved path, so it blocked the whole card.

- tools/dev_test_tool.py: `dev_test_run` (kanban toolset, dispatcher-owned
  workers only). Typed arguments (profile, approved package patterns, -run
  regex, race/short/vet, bounded timeout); no URL, env or go flag can be
  passed. Every call re-verifies the root-owned profile registry and the
  root-owned runner (owner, mode, no symlink, root-owned parents, pinned
  SHA-256), scans the exact fixed invocation through the normal guards
  (nothing filtered) and runs it with an empty environment; the runner
  re-checks the board claim (its parent must be the worker pid of the
  running claim) and the repository lease, then sandboxes the tests.
- Scanner recovery: an unattended rejection of a go test/vet command that
  matches a registered profile carries a RECOVERY directive naming
  dev_test_run; kanban_block refuses until that equivalent was tried.
- Guards (additive): commands that read a registered test credential file
  or enter/inspect its container are blocked under every mode (also file
  tools); unattended deny mode refuses non-loopback database targets and
  passwords written into a command line.

Tirith stays enabled and fail-closed, single-query/cron/unattended modes
stay deny, hardline and deny rules are unchanged.
